 <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d={arrow} /></svg>
 </a>
 </div>
 </div>
 </div>
 </div>
 </section>

 <!-- ════ Industry 4: Roofing & Solar — paper ════ -->
 <section id="industry-roofing-solar" class="scroll-mt-20 border-y border-hairline bg-paper py-20 sm:py-28">
 <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
 <div class="grid items-start gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[auto_1fr]">
 <div class="h-20 w-20 flex-shrink-0 overflow-hidden border border-hairline sm:h-28 sm:w-28">
 <img
 src="/images/generated/kit-roofing.jpg"
 alt="Roofing crew gear — ANSI hi-vis tee, embroidered bucket hat, hoodie"
 width="400"
 height="400"
 loading="lazy"
 decoding="async"
 class="h-full w-full object-cover"
 />
 </div>
 <div>
 <span class="spec mb-3 inline-block text-gold-600">Roofing & Solar</span>
 <h2 class="font-heading text-3xl font-extrabold uppercase leading-[0.95] tracking-tight text-charcoal sm:text-4xl">
 Hi-vis on every rooftop. Sun-proof gear for 115-degree Vegas summers.
 </h2>
 <div class="mt-5 space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ash">
 <p>
 Roofing and solar employers must assess each work zone and select required visibility apparel. Bighorn can quote selected tees, long-sleeves, hoodies, and vests. The employer and manufacturer must approve any regulated garment and decoration plan.
 </p>
 <p>
 Las Vegas roof work can create serious heat and sun exposure. The employer's heat plan controls apparel choices. Bighorn can quote products with published UPF ratings, plus compatible hats, jackets, booth apparel, and promotional items.
 </p>
 <p>
 Common orders: hi-vis ANSI tees and hoodies, UPF long-sleeves, custom hard hats, embroidered sales-rep softshells, trade show giveaways, and branded safety vests.
 </p>
 </div>
 <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
 {['ANSI Class 2/3 Hi-Vis', 'UPF 30+ Long-Sleeves', 'Custom Hard Hats', 'Sales Rep Softshells', 'Trade Show Swag', 'Branded Trucker Hats', 'Safety Vests'].map((tag) => (
 <span class="spec border border-hairline px-2.5 py-1 text-ash">{tag}</span>
 ))}
